      "text": "In fact, he did not file any appeal against his conviction.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 4058,
      "end": 4117,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3297169506549835
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 35,
      "text": "8. The present appellant who is the brother-in-law of the deceased is here before us with this appeal.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 4119,
      "end": 4221,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 36,
      "text": "9. We have heard Mr. Bharat Bhushan, the learned counsel appearing for the appellant and Mr. K.\nParmeshwar, the learned senior counsel appearing for the State of Uttar Pradesh.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 4223,
      "end": 4399,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Bharat Bhushan",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 4244,
          "end": 4258
        },
        {
          "text": "K.\nParmeshwar",
          "label": "LAWYER",
          "start": 4316,
          "end": 4329
        },
        {
          "text": "State of Uttar Pradesh",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 4376,
          "end": 4398
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 37,
      "text": "10. We have looked into the oral evidence on record.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 4401,
      "end": 4453,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 38,
      "text": "We have also looked into the nature of the allegations levelled against the appellant herein.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4454,
      "end": 4547,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.11464861780405045
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 39,
      "text": "11. We are of the view that there is practically no evidence on the basis of which it could be said that the appellant herein as brother-in-law abetted the commission of suicide.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4549,
      "end": 4727,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.356524795293808
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 40,
      "text": "We need not say anything further in the matter.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4728,
      "end": 4775,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.04079502448439598
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 41,
      "text": "Ram Pyarey vs The State Of Uttar Pradesh on 9 January, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/179427786/\n2",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4776,
      "end": 4893,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Ram Pyarey vs The State Of Uttar Pradesh on 9 January, 2025 Indian Kanoon",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 4777,
          "end": 4850
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.4900416135787964
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 42,
      "text": "12. The law as regards the abetment of suicide punishable under Sections 306 of the IPC is now well settled.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4894,
      "end": 5002,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Sections 306",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 4958,
          "end": 4970
        },
        {
          "text": "IPC",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 4978,
          "end": 4981
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.1948998123407364
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 43,
      "text": "It appears that the Courts below laid much emphasis on Section 113B of the Evidence Act,\n1872 (for short, the Evidence Act).",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 5003,
      "end": 5127,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 113B",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 5058,
          "end": 5070
        },
        {
          "text": "Evidence Act,\n1872",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 5078,
          "end": 5096
        },
        {
          "text": "Evidence Act",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 5113,
          "end": 5125
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.08502094447612762
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 44,
      "text": "Section 113A of the Evidence Act talks about presumption.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 5128,
      "end": 5185,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 113A",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 5128,
          "end": 5140
        },
        {
          "text": "Evidence Act",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 5148,
          "end": 5160
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.12328439950942993
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 45,
      "text": "Section 113A and Section 113B read thus:-\n113A. Presumption as to abetment of suicide by a married woman.",
      "rhetorical_role": "STA",
      "start": 5186,
      "end": 5292,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 113A",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 5187,
          "end": 5199
        },
        {
          "text": "Section 113B",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 5204,
          "end": 5216
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.16641905903816223
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 46,
      "text": "When the question is whether the commission of suicide by a woman had been abetted by her husband or any relative of her husband and it is shown that she had committed suicide within a period of seven years from the date of her marriage and that her husband or such relative of her husband had subjected her to cruelty, the Court may presume, having regard to all the other circumstances of the case, that such suicide had been abetted by her husband or by such relative of her husband.",
      "rhetorical_role": "STA",
      "start": 5293,
      "end": 5779,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3084951341152191
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 47,
      "text": "Explanation.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 5781,
      "end": 5793,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.06715802103281021
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 48,
      "text": "For the purposes of this section, cruelty shall have the same meaning as in section 498A of the Indian Penal Code (45 of 1860).",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 5794,
      "end": 5921,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "section 498A",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 5870,
          "end": 5882
        },
        {
          "text": "Indian Penal Code (45 of 1860)",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 5890,
          "end": 5920
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2074478715658188
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 49,
      "text": "113B. Presumption as to dowry death.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 5922,
      "end": 5959,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.19738087058067322
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 50,
      "text": "When the question is whether a person has committed the dowry death of a woman and it is shown that soon before her death such woman had been subjected by such person to cruelty or harassment for, or in connection with, any demand for dowry, the Court shall presume that such person had caused the dowry death.",
      "rhetorical_role": "STA",
      "start": 5960,
      "end": 6270,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2596948742866516
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 51,
      "text": "Explanation.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 6272,
      "end": 6284,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.07183568179607391
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 52,
      "text": "For the purposes of this section, dowry death shall have the same meaning as in section 304B of the Indian Penal Code (45 of 1860).",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 6285,
      "end": 6416,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "section 304B",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 6365,
          "end": 6377
        },
        {
          "text": "Indian Penal Code (45 of 1860)",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 6385,
          "end": 6415
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.14023573696613312
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 53,
      "text": "13. It is relevant to note that under Section 113B, the Court may presume unlike Section 113A where the statute says that Court shall presume.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 6418,
      "end": 6560,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 113B",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 6456,
          "end": 6468
        },
        {
          "text": "Section 113A",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 6499,
          "end": 6511
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.11162416636943817
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 54,
      "text": "This is a vital difference between the two provisions which raises presumption as regards abetment of suicide.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 6561,
      "end": 6671,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.4685048758983612
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 55,
      "text": "When the Courts below want to apply Section 113B of the Evidence Act, the condition precedent is that there has to be first some cogent evidence as regards incessant harassment.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 6672,
      "end": 6849,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 113B",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 6708,
          "end": 6720
        },
        {
          "text": "Evidence Act",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 6728,
          "end": 6740
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.5705995559692383
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 56,
      "text": "In the absence of any cogent evidence as regards harassment or abetment in any form like aiding or instigating, the court cannot straightaway invoke Section 113B and presume that the accused abetted the commission of suicide.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 6850,
      "end": 7075,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 113B",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 6999,
          "end": 7011
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.5925970077514648
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 57,
      "text": "14. In view of the aforesaid, this appeal succeeds and is hereby allowed.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 7077,
      "end": 7150,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.02967173606157303
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 58,
      "text": "The judgment and order of conviction passed by the trial court as confirmed by the High Court is hereby set aside.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 7151,
      "end": 7265,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.1474582850933075
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 59,
      "text": "15. The appellant is already on bail.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 7267,
      "end": 7304,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.14765532314777374
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 60,
      "text": "His bail bonds stand discharged.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 7305,
      "end": 7337,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.1227702721953392
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 61,
      "text": "16. Pending application(s), if any, stands disposed of.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 7338,
      "end": 7394,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.07874426245689392
